<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who the Sport Edition is for</h2>
        <p>The Sport Edition is Nordic's recovery-focused series, for runners, skiers, cyclists, lifters, and anyone whose back and legs take a beating. Nordic Star jets deliver pulsating hot water therapy aimed at the back, legs and feet. With models from the 2-person D'Amour SE to the 6-person Encore SE and Jubilee SE, you can size it for a couple or a family. The 3-person Stella SE is a compact option for entertaining with a 3-hp pump.</p>
        <h2>Electrical and installation</h2>
        <p>Nordic lists the Encore SE, Retreat SE and Stella SE at 220V/40A, so plan on a dedicated circuit from a licensed electrician. Capacities run from about 240 gallons (Stella SE) to 330 gallons (Encore SE), which makes these spas quicker to fill and heat than larger family models. A level concrete pad, compacted gravel base or engineered deck works. See <a href="/guides/110v-vs-240v-hot-tubs/">110V vs 240V</a> and our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-cost-utah/">cost guide</a>.</p>
        <h2>Recovery through a Utah winter</h2>
        <p>Winter is prime recovery season after ski days. Sport Edition spas come with foam insulation, and Nordic offers the Nordic Wrap upgrade (R-9.5, per the manufacturer) for extra protection in the cold. Keep the cover locked down between soaks. See our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a> and our <a href="/health-wellness/">health &amp; wellness</a> page.</p>
        <h2>See the Sport Edition in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

